    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10-a4">

                <pb facs="0101" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg21"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Agreement</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">for
                        collocation of boundary marks</hi>).</head>
                <dateline>[<placeName>Santiago</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1902-05-28">May 28, 1902</date>]</dateline>
                <p>Met together in the ministry for foreign relations of Chile, the minister of that
                    department, Señor Don José Francisco Vergara Donoso, and the envoy extraordinary
                    and minister plenipotentiary of the Argentine Republic, Señor Don José Antonio
                    Terry, duly authorized and acting in accordance with the boundary treaty of July
                    23, 1881, the protocol of May 1, 1893, the agreement of April 17, 1896, and the
                    acts <pb facs="0102" n="22" xml:id="pg22"/> of September 15, 17, and 22, 1898,
                    in order to avoid any difficulty in the actual demarkation of the boundary line
                    between the two countries in the first part submitted to the decision of His
                    Brittanic Majesty, do agree, in the name of their respective Governments, to ask
                    the arbitrator to name a commission which shall fix in the territory in question
                    the boundary marks which he shall order in his decision. In witness whereof they
                    sign this agreement in duplicate, in Santiago, the 28th day of May, 1902.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. Terry.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. F. Vergara Donoso.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
